--- /dev/null
+++ b/llmdocs/NIBI_SUBMISSION.md
@@ -0,0 +1,208 @@
+# Nibi submission package — SDOML sweep + new-model benchmarks (2026-07-24)
+
+Prepared on the dev box (platogpu007, no `sbatch` here — nothing was or could
+be submitted from this box). Everything below runs on a **Nibi login node**.
+
+Payloads:
+
+1. **SDOML sparsity sweep** (`sbatch/run_sdoml_sweep.sh`, new) — fills every
+   missing SDOML cell of `tab:sparse` / `tab:bpw_sparse`
+   (tracker `llmdocs/tracker/RERUN_2026-07-22_paper_doml_sdoml.md` §D):
+   s ∈ {5,20,25,40,50,75} on Qwen3-1.7B AND Llama-3.2-1B via the full honest
+   container chain (dump → honest bpw → block-tune fp8 → assign-tune pair →
+   honest bpw → restore + full eval), plus SDOML+partition asymmetric
+   s ∈ {20,50} on both models via the house `run.py sdoml_partition
+   --sdoml_asymmetric --full_eval` path. **16 jobs.**
+2. **New-model benchmarks** (`sbatch/run_smollm2_1.7b_benchmark.sh`,
+   `run_olmo2_1b_benchmark.sh`, `run_granite_3.3_2b_benchmark.sh`, all new;
+   Falcon3 dropped 2026-07-24 — verdict decided on the dev box, TQ wins it; kyutai/helium-1-2b dropped 2026-07-24 — released checkpoint unusable, FP16 baseline wt2 418 on the dev box, replaced by ibm-granite/granite-3.3-2b-base which uses the repo's native granite plumbing) — per model: (a) the DOML K31 honest
+   chain (build λ/g256/fp8-cb/hdiag/intra-block-GPTQ/refit2/bulk-K2/rd-split →
+   k31_block_tune → k31_assign_tune pair → k29_honest_bpw → restore +
+   full eval) and (b) TesseraQ paper-exact (bit 2, gs 128, iters 250, bsz 4,
+   nsamples 512, seed 0, `--full_eval`). **6 jobs.**
+3. **AWQ arm** (`sbatch/run_smollm2_1.7b_awq_benchmark.sh`,
+   `run_granite_3.3_2b_awq_benchmark.sh`, new 2026-07-24 evening) — the SAME
+   honest DOML K31 chain with the AWQ v1 activation-scaling transform
+   (`CRB_AWQ_ALPHA=0.5`, committed machinery) applied at build; motivated by
+   the Falcon3 root-cause finding (activation-outlier ratio predicts AWQ
+   applicability from calib data alone). Fully collision-proof vs the non-AWQ
+   arm: dump dirs `awqfix05-*` (vs `k31-*`), CSVs
+   `results/<model>_awq_ptq_benchmark.csv` (separate files), job names
+   `<model>_doml_awq` (separate logs), separate SLURM allocations; no
+   tesseraq duplicate. **OLMo2 deliberately has NO AWQ arm** — Olmo2 is
+   norm-AFTER (its decoder layer has no `input_layernorm` feeding q/k/v), so
+   the v1 fold is mathematically inapplicable; running it would either crash
+   or silently change the model function. **2 jobs.**
+
+**Total: 24 sbatch jobs.**
+
+---
+
+## 0. What must be on Nibi first — the sync patch is NOT optional
+
+**Sync routes (pick ONE, 2026-07-24 evening rev):** commit `7634dea`
+("Mo models") now carries most campaign changes. If your Nibi checkout can
+`git pull` to `7634dea`: apply only **`nibi_delta.patch`** (6 diffs:
+helium→granite swap, `download_cache.sh`, this doc, the
+`src/run_tesseraq.py` granite fix, and the 2 new AWQ sbatch scripts). If your
+checkout is at `6675f49` ("New DOML") with no way to pull: apply the full
+**`nibi_sync.patch`**. Do not apply both.
+
+**`src/run_tesseraq.py` granite fix is NOT optional for the granite tesseraq
+job:** without it `get_model` rejects `ibm-granite/granite-3.3-2b-base`
+(`ValueError: Unsupported model`) — observed live on the dev box, died in 5 s.
+The fix adds a granite loader branch and maps `GraniteForCausalLM` onto the
+llama block layout (same module names; granite's scalar multipliers live
+inside `forward`). Both patches now carry it.
+
+Historical context — the dev-box tree previously carried **uncommitted**
+changes that every job here depends on: the new-model family mappings in `run.py` / `src/eval_utils.py` /
+`src/run_tesseraq.py` (without them every smollm2/olmo2 job dies
+with `ValueError: Unsupported model` — the SmolLM2 TesseraQ crash was observed
+live on the dev box pre-fix), the `Salesforce/wikitext` dataset namespacing in
+`datautils.py`, the `CRB_REPO` repo-root fix in all `kernels/pack/*` tools
+(they previously hardcoded `/workspace/BiLLM2`), and the `--full-eval`
+downstream passthrough on both restore-eval paths. `nibi_sync.patch` carries
+the full working-tree diff **plus** the untracked files the jobs need
+(`kernels/pack/awq_transform.py`, the five new sbatch scripts, this document).
+It applies cleanly ONLY on commit `6675f49` ("New DOML") — verified against a
+pristine clone on the dev box.
+
+`kernels/pack/awq_transform.py` note: `run.py` imports it **lazily**, only
+inside branches gated on `CRB_AWQ_ALPHA` / `CRB_AWQ_V2` /
+`--salient_metric actmag`. None of the 22 jobs sets those, so it is not on any
+job's import path — it ships anyway so the patched `run.py` can never hit a
+missing-module edge on Nibi.
+
+## 1. Login-node steps, in order
+
+```bash
+cd ~/CRB   # (wherever the Nibi checkout lives; repo root, NOT sbatch/)
+
+# 1. Bring the checkout to the commit the patch was cut against.
+git fetch origin
+git checkout main
+git pull                      # must land on 6675f49 "New DOML"
+git rev-parse HEAD            # -> 6675f49e8a1595aebfd8344aa8fad20885a23a49
+git status --porcelain        # must be EMPTY; stash/clean local edits first
+
+# 2. Copy the patch from the dev box and apply it.
+#    (scp platogpu007:/workspace/CRB/nibi_sync.patch .)
+git apply --stat  nibi_sync.patch   # review: 34 diffs (26 modified + 8 new files)
+git apply --check nibi_sync.patch   # must print nothing
+git apply nibi_sync.patch
+ls -la sbatch/run_sdoml_sweep.sh    # new scripts arrive executable (100755)
+
+# 3. Refresh the offline caches (login node has internet; compute nodes do
+#    not). Fetches the four new models, warms the NAMESPACED
+#    Salesforce/wikitext dataset id the patched datautils now requests, and
+#    verifies Olmo2/Granite transformers support before any GPU time is spent.
+#    .hf_token handling is unchanged (read from ./.hf_token if present; the
+#    four new models are ungated and need no token).
+./sbatch/download_cache.sh
+
+# 4. Submit. Replace def-xxx with the usual account.
+./sbatch/run_sdoml_sweep.sh          --account def-xxx   # 16 jobs
+./sbatch/run_smollm2_1.7b_benchmark.sh --account def-xxx #  2 jobs
+./sbatch/run_olmo2_1b_benchmark.sh   --account def-xxx   #  2 jobs
+./sbatch/run_granite_3.3_2b_benchmark.sh --account def-xxx #  2 jobs
+./sbatch/run_smollm2_1.7b_awq_benchmark.sh --account def-xxx #  1 job (AWQ arm)
+./sbatch/run_granite_3.3_2b_awq_benchmark.sh --account def-xxx #  1 job (AWQ arm)
+```
+
