+
+GRES strings are the full long-form MIG names (`nvidia_h100_80gb_hbm3_2g.20gb`
+etc.) copied verbatim from the proven house scripts; `4g.40gb` is NOT
+provisioned on Nibi (Gotcha #33) and is not used anywhere.
+
+Sizing rationale (dev-box measurements, never undercut):
+
+- **SDOML/DOML chains on 3g.40gb, not 2g.20gb:** assignment-tune used
+  29–35 GB on the old A40s, OOM'd a 24 GB slice for Llama-3.2-1B even at
+  batch4 (tracker incidents), and the DOML 1B-class chain envelope was proven
+  at 24 GB with the batch2 (smollm2: batch4) knobs the scripts pin. 20 GB
+  undercuts every proven envelope; 3g.40gb (40 GB) is the smallest Nibi slice
+  at or above it. The 2g.20gb house precedent covered only single-stage
+  `run.py sdoml`/`doml` jobs, not the tune chain.
+- **λ (new models, PROVISIONAL, parameterized at the top of each script):**
+  smollm2 32e-5, olmo2 19e-5, granite 16e-5 — current best-known
+  rate-matched picks from the dev-box arms (smollm2/granite still settling locally). Re-pick only if a Nibi honest-bpw log lands far off ≤2.25-class.
+- **SDOML has no λ and no g256 stage:** `--rd-split` is a DOML-build knob the
+  SDOML chain does not have, and the g256 codebook refit was measured a dead
+  end for SDOML (`SDOML_honest_frontier.md` §9). The paper SDOML recipe is
+  g128 + fp8 codebooks (via block-tune) + assignment-tune, which is exactly
+  what the sweep runs.
+- **TesseraQ on full h100 + 160G:** dev-box peak >23.6 GB GPU (OOMed a 24 GB
+  slice) and >100 GB RSS; house precedent for this size class (Qwen3-1.7B /
+  Llama-3.2-1B tesseraq) is GPU_FULL + 160G + 28 h — kept ×1, not shrunk.
+
+## 3. Where results land
+
+- **CSVs** (fcntl-locked appends, one row per (task, metric)):
+  - SDOML sweep: `results/sdoml_sweep_<model>_<config>.csv` — one CSV per job,
+    deliberately separate from the April `*_ptq_benchmark.csv` files so rerun
+    cells never mix with old rows.
+  - New models: `results/<model_short>_ptq_benchmark.csv` (house convention;
+    these models never ran on Nibi, so the names are collision-free).
+  - AWQ arm: `results/<model_short>_awq_ptq_benchmark.csv` — deliberately a
+    SEPARATE file per model so AWQ rows can never mix with the plain-DOML rows
+    (both arms write method-tag `doml`; the file is the discriminator).
+    Containers land in `…/doml_dumps/<model>/awqfix05-…[-btuned|-atuned]`,
+    disjoint from the `k31-…` plain dumps. The `awqfix05-*` dump dirs carry an
+    `awq_scales.safetensors` the restore/tune stages REQUIRE — never delete it
+    or mix containers across arms.
+- **Honest bpw**: printed in the job `.out` log —
+  `grep -h "HONEST bpw" logs/*sdoml-s*_*.out logs/*_doml_*.out`
+  (SDOML jobs print it twice: base bf16 reference, then FINAL fp8 container —
+  the FINAL one is the `tab:bpw_sparse` number).
+- **Containers**: `$SCRATCH/billm2_cache/downloads/doml_dumps/<model>/...`
+  (`sdoml-sNN[-btuned|-atuned]`, `k31-<tag>-lam<λ>-g256[-btuned|-atuned]`).
+  Expect a few GB per model — fine on scratch. Chain stages are idempotent
+  (skip on existing `manifest.json`), so a TIME-LIMIT or requeued job can
+  simply be resubmitted and resumes past finished stages.
+- **atune fallback**: if assignment-tune fails (its memory profile is the
+  chain's highest), the job logs a WARN and ships the **btuned** container —
+  tracker precedent: still a complete honest DOML/SDOML row. Check for
+  `WARN: .*assign_tune failed` in `.out` logs to know which rows shipped
+  btuned.
+
+## 4. Open risks / things I could not verify from the dev box
+
+1. **SLURM specifics** (module names `gcc arrow scipy-stack cuda cudnn`, GRES
+   strings, b1–b5 walltime tiers, `--parsable` behavior) are copied verbatim
+   from the proven April scripts — there is no `sbatch`/`sinfo` on this box to
+   re-confirm the cluster still advertises them.
+2. **Nibi venv transformers version**: April jobs proved ≥4.51 (Qwen3 guard).
+   OLMo-2 needs ≥4.47, Granite is long-supported — expected satisfied, but not verifiable
+   from here. Both `download_cache.sh` and the per-job guards abort cleanly
+   (before GPU time) if not.
+3. **Granite-3.3-2b substitution (2026-07-24):** replaces kyutai/helium-1-2b, whose
+   released checkpoint is unusable in-stack (FP16 baseline wt2 418 measured on the
+   dev box — model broken as shipped, not harness/DOML). Granite uses the repo's
+   long-standing native granite plumbing; λ=16e-5 provisional (local arm running).
+4. **SDOML+partition asymmetric honest bpw**: there is NO container/honest-bpw
+   tooling for the asymmetric arm (the frontier doc dead-ended it as an
+   iterable vehicle). These 4 jobs produce PPL + downstream via the exact May
+   command; the bpw for `tab:bpw_sparse` stays the analytic `eq:bpw_asym`
+   value (2.51 / 2.09 at d_in=2048). Building an asym container tool remains
+   an open item — flagged, not silently absorbed.
+5. **Walltimes for the chain jobs** (10 h / 14 h) are dev-box walls with ≥2×
+   margin for the slower per-SM Nibi MIG slices, not measured-on-Nibi numbers.
+   Chains are idempotent, so a TIME LIMIT costs a resubmit, not the work done.
+6. **Datasets cache staleness**: the namespaced `Salesforce/wikitext` warm in
+   `download_cache.sh` must run BEFORE any new-model job (Step 3 ordering);
+   existing Qwen/Llama tokenized `.pt` caches are unaffected.
